  "cases_description": "The object above is the ORIGINAL single case and carries `metadata: null`. From the Olanote change onward the calendar module always attaches `{\"olanote\": {\"auto_join\": ...}}`, plus any keys another system wrote, so that shape is retired in production and a vector covering only it would pin a case that can no longer occur. These cases cover the shapes that are actually sent. Every one was produced by meeting-api's own `parse_entry` (the producer owns the contract); the calendar module must reproduce each `content_hash` from the same `raw_input`. The last case exists because `sort_keys` has to recurse into nested objects: it is the property most likely to break if either side ever swaps its serialiser.",
